SUM OF SUBARRAY MINIMUMS
(LeetCode 907) - REVISION NOTES
===========================

---------------------------------------------------
CORE IDEA
---------------------------------------------------

Instead of finding the minimum for every subarray,

Find:

"For each element, in how many subarrays is it the minimum?"

Contribution of every element:

Contribution = Frequency × Element

Final Answer = Sum of all Contributions

---------------------------------------------------
FORMULAS
---------------------------------------------------

left = i - PSEE
→ Number of possible starting positions.

right = NSE - i
→ Number of possible ending positions.

frequency = left × right
→ Number of subarrays where arr[i] is the minimum.

contribution = frequency × arr[i]

answer = (answer + contribution) % mod

---------------------------------------------------
WHY LEFT × RIGHT ?
---------------------------------------------------

Every valid starting index can combine with every valid ending index.

Example

Starts : 2 choices

Ends : 3 choices

Possible subarrays

2 × 3 = 6

Hence,

frequency = left × right

---------------------------------------------------
PSEE (Previous Smaller or Equal Element)
---------------------------------------------------

Traverse Left → Right

while(arr[stackTop] > arr[i])

Store:

Previous Smaller OR Equal Index

If not found

Store

-1

Reason:

Imaginary index before the array.

Formula:

left = i - (-1)

---------------------------------------------------
NSE (Next Smaller Element)
---------------------------------------------------

Traverse Right → Left

while(arr[stackTop] >= arr[i])

Store:

Next Smaller Index

If not found

Store

n

Reason:

Imaginary index after the array.

Formula:

right = n - i

---------------------------------------------------
WHY >= IN NSE ?
---------------------------------------------------

Pop greater or equal elements.

This keeps only the next STRICTLY smaller element.

---------------------------------------------------
WHY > IN PSEE ?
---------------------------------------------------

Pop only greater elements.

Equal elements remain.

Reason:

Avoid duplicate counting.

---------------------------------------------------
WHY STORE INDICES IN STACK?
---------------------------------------------------

Stack stores:

INDEX

NOT VALUE

Because later we need

left = i - psee[i]

right = nse[i] - i

These require positions (indices), not values.

